WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.350
Headmaster, how's gathering materials 
for the barrier coming?

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.640
I wish I could say 
it was coming smoothly, but...

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.250
Not enough Crests of Glory?

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.390
Yes.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:16.910
Most of the Crests of Glory in the kingdom 
are enrolled at the First Academy.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.910
Couldn't we ask First Academy 
for help, then?

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.990
That would be difficult.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.670
First and Second Academies 
have never really gotten along.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.880
But I suppose things are too dire 
to indulge in old rivalries.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.710
I'll ask His Majesty to intervene.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.590
This is absurd!

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:41.850
The headmaster of the inferior Second Academy 
has no right to summon me!

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.410
As my subordinate, 
you should come to me!

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.600
His Majesty ordered this.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.950
And as far as I know, 
there's no hierarchy

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.320
between the headmasters 
of our two academies.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.760
No hierarchy?!

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.500
Our superiority is clear 
from our Crest of Glory numbers!

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.290
<i>I'm getting déjà vu from this guy.</i>

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.780
Can we drop the hogwash 
and get to the matter at hand?

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.710
"Hogwash"?!

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:11.470
It's about the barrier we're putting up 
over the kingdom to keep out the demons.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:16.050
I want the aid of the First Academy's 
Crest of Glory users in refining the ore.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.680
I refuse!

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.660
The prestigious First Academy, 
working with the inferior Second Academy?!

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.940
It's about time you reevaluated 
your views on the crests.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.690
We proved ourselves at the
inter-school competition, didn't we?

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:32.440
The results of that match were negated 
due to demonic interference!

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.810
Hey, now...

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:37.660
The "demonic interference" 
was one of your students!

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.550
Well, here's an idea.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.220
Why don't we redo the competition?

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.890
Each side can decide 
how many people to send.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.580
The loser does whatever the winner asks.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.830
How about that?

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.360
I like it.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.020
But I have a condition as well!

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.420
A condition?

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.810
That beast is forbidden to participate!

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.720
As are the members of his party!

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.140
Excuse me, that's—

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.230
Fine by me.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.520
The competition will be in two days' time!

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:11.060
And I will overturn these slanderous claims 
about First Academy's loss!

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.270
Just you wait!

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:14.860
Whoops...

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.990
Can we win under these circumstances?

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.700
Absolutely. Let's shut them up 
once and for all.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.000
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:59.000
<b>The Strongest Sage Makes Allies.</b>

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.970
Heaven's sake...

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.410
First Academy really went all-out.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:15.580
<i>I'd planned to send Iris in 
if any of them seemed dangerous,</i>

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.880
<i>but I don't sense any demons here.</i>

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.940
<i>No need for Iris this time, I think.</i>

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.530
I can't believe you showed your faces!

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.310
Why wouldn't we?

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.450
We have no need to run from you.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:34.350
Our participants are our academy's 
finest Crest of Glory students.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.170
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.740
Fight with all you have!

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.780
Sir!

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.120
And? What about Second Academy?

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.600
They're coming out now.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.050
Wh-What?!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:51.270
A mere five of them?!

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.030
One Crest of Failure,

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:54.360
two Crests of Standard,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.010
and two Crests of Lesser.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.420
You mock me at every turn!

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.900
Are we going to talk, 
or are we going to start?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.360
Very well.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.740
The result is predetermined!

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.740
Make-up Inter-Academy Competition...

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:08.970
Begin!

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.620
Magic of flame that dwells within me—

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.520
Wordless casting?!

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.000
Are you kidding me?!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.590
Wh-What's wrong with you?!

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.750
There are only five of them!

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:32.060
Match over!

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.100
Winner, Second Academy!

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.440
<i>Even five was too many, I guess.</i>

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.380
Impossible!

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:41.850
I refuse to accept this result!

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:42.610
Why?

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.010
They're all obviously beasts!

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:47.110
I told you, no beasts!

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:51.240
Those children may be some 
of our best students,

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:55.070
but their ability is not 
significantly greater than any other.

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:57.740
Prove it, then!

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.240
I'm not sure how to do that.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.160
Let her fight, then!

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.520
Me?

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.470
Sure, but I didn't bring a weapon.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.830
Try this.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.460
Hey, when did you get my sword?

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:14.370
Hold on!

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.050
Let me look that over! 
To make sure there are no tricks.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:18.350
As you wish.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.290
A shoddy little blade...

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:23.560
Truly appropriate for Second Academy!

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.340
Iris?

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:26.260
Right.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.410
H-Hey, be careful with that!

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.330
Sh-She's a beast!

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.840
What a mean thing to say!

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.830
I'm a girl!

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.040
<i>A dragon one, of course...</i>

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.440
By the way, Facus...

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.230
Wh-What now?!

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:49.130
His Majesty ordered us 
to switch to wordless casting.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.950
But First Academy is still using 
incanted spells!

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.850
What is the meaning of this?

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.290
What's wrong with that?

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.560
I must protect this kingdom's 
educational principles

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.160
from pathetic Crests of Failure 
and mediocre Crests of Standard!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.970
Even if it is His Majesty's order—

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:07.360
You refuse the command of your king, then?

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.780
Y-Your Majesty!

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.370
I-It was just a figure of speech!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.510
I certainly didn't mean—

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.280
Royal guard! Seize this traitor!

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:20.900
W-Wait!

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:23.160
Your Majesty! Your Majesty!

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.620
Curse you, Second Academy!

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.580
You trapped me!

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:30.590
You'll pay! You'll pay!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:35.180
Now, students of my Royal First Academy!

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:39.180
From this moment forward, 
you will work with Second Academy,

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.610
receive education in wordless casting,

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.980
and assist them with the plan in progress!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.620
Any objections!

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.640
No, sir!

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:51.530
Bringing in the king was the right call.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.120
Indeed.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:01.460
I'm glad First Academy students 
were all so cooperative.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.330
They must've really hated that headmaster.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.120
No kidding!

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.470
We'll be able to make up 
the barrier at this rate.

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:11.010
And wordless casting should 
gain even more traction.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.140
Where are we going today?

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:15.050
Gathering materials for the barrier.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.470
For the barrier? 
Like mithril?

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:20.960
That's for the students 
of First Academy to handle.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.600
We're going to get a magistone!

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.940
To form the barrier's core, yes?

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.570
But we need a 60-centimeter one 
for that, right?

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:31.960
It shouldn't be that hard.

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:33.720
For instance...

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:41.790
Er, could you please not look at me 
while discussing magistones?!

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:45.920
Iris is a dragon, so she likely has 
a magistone exceeding 80 centimeters.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:47.490
No way...

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:48.920
You're going to take it from Iris?!

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.590
Don't worry. I won't do that.

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.530
There's another way to get one.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.430
We're going to summon a monster!

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.810
<i>Alma and Lurie are coming along nicely,</i>

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:11.570
<i>but Iris is still a problem.</i>

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.320
<i>Her control over her own power is poor.</i>

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:25.000
<i>So this will partly be a test to see 
if she has what it takes to join our party.</i>

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:28.420
<i>Give it your best, okay?</i>

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:32.060
This is my first time on the 17th floor!

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.050
Me, too!

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.440
Really?

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:39.890
Someone I used to know made it 
all the way down to the 654th floor.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.010
<i>She means me in my past life.</i>

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.460
We'll summon the monster here.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:54.140
Lurie, could you form a casting circle 
around this magistone?

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.440
I'll try!

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.320
Go for it, Lurie!

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:11.800
This is rather difficult.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.000
Calm down. You can do this.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.090
Here, I'll support you.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.930
S-Sorry... I'll concentrate.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.590
I did it!

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:26.890
Great work! You're getting better 
and better at this, Lurie.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:30.360
Th-Thank you so much...

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:34.120
Gettin' hot in here, ain't it, Iris?

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:39.250
Iris! Infuse this with magic, 
if you would.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.580
Sure.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:43.710
Too much at once could lead 
to disaster, so do it slowly.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.870
"Slowly," huh?

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.000
Here I go...

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.020
Slowly... slowly...

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.850
Wait a minute! That's too—

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:58.130
Too little?

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.020
I'll ramp it up, then!

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.520
Not up! <i>Down</i>!

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:05.640
Actually, call it off!

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.600
A-All right!

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:11.790
It's too late.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:15.320
We might summon a monster 
beyond what this floor can handle!

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.280
It's coming down! Run!

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:23.410
Iris! I told you 
to infuse it with magic <i>slowly</i>!

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.450
I did! I infused it very slowly!

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.290
How could anyone call that "slowly"?!

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:33.170
Well, I once knew someone who said, 
"I'm going to give my casting a little test,"

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.250
and then blew up three mountains...

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.050
Don't confuse me 
with someone so reckle—

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:43.400
Are you talking about me?

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.140
Yes. In your past life as Gaius.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.590
Is that... a dragon?

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:06.600
Yeah, it should give up 
a 60-centimeter magistone easily.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.340
Iris, you take the lead.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:09.260
Right!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.540
Here I go!

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:13.870
Iris!

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:18.830
Hey! No fair attacking 
out of the blue like that!

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:22.020
Iris. Can you talk him down?

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:24.440
Talk him down? How?

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:25.840
Let's see...

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.890
What? No way!

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.060
Just do it.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:34.350
Fine...

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.580
Hey, you winged lizard!

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.360
Just die already!

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:43.010
I will kill you.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.900
Is she supposed to be talking him down?

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:48.170
What did she say?

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:49.760
She called him a "winged lizard."

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.830
It's the most offensive thing 
you can say to a dragon.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.970
That's not talking him down! 
It's riling him up!

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:58.980
Iris! 
Keep drawing the dragon's attention!

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:01.560
What am I, the bait?!

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.260
Not the bait! A diversion!

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.010
Isn't that the same thing?!

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.010
Lurie! Now!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.200
R-Right!

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:09.340
Alma!

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:10.520
I'm on it!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.230
It's not dealing any damage!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.530
That's okay! Just keep it up!

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:24.360
<i>In the meantime, 
I'll set up the casting circles!</i>

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.780
It noticed us!

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.740
Iris! Protect them!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.690
Very well!

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:38.120
Put those eyes where they belong!

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:45.970
He's not very strong 
for such a big fellow, is he?

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.820
Iris is in a slugfest with a dragon!

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:59.240
It almost feels unreal.

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:01.230
Keep those attacks coming, you two!

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.780
That attack won't work on me!

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:09.990
Iris, when attacks come from above, 
you should dodge them!

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:10.700
Eh?

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.330
Iris!

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:17.200
<i>Good grief...</i>

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:24.000
The ground in these higher dungeon floors 
is awfully brittle...

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.600
That's why you shouldn't 
just block every hit.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:31.050
Say, it's kinda weird how he
hasn't used Dragon's Breath, huh?

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.830
I'm using my magic to block it.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:36.440
Oh, is that why?

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:39.330
<i>Dragon bodies are tough.</i>

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.360
<i>You can't penetrate them with arrows,</i>

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:44.150
<i>and they're not vulnerable 
to the toxins I used on those demons.</i>

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.420
<i>I could have Iris turn 
into a dragon to fight it,</i>

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:49.380
<i>but that would be a lot 
to put on her shoulders right now,</i>

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:51.340
<i>and she probably couldn't control 
her power properly.</i>

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:56.450
<i>Annoying as it is, 
this is the only reliable way to beat it!</i>

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:59.120
Okay! We're ready to go!

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.630
Get away from it, you two!

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:01.330
Very well!

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:01.960
Got it!

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.210
Iris! How many seconds 
do you need to get away?

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.960
Four seconds, I guess... 
But I'd prefer to have five!

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:11.900
Right! See if you can get it 
to use its Dragon's Breath!

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.650
Very well!

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:18.510
Hey! You can't even use 
one measly Dragon's Breath?!

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:21.740
I guess you really are just a winged lizard!

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:26.100
You... 
If you wish to die that badly...

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.790
Then die!

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.150
Nice work, Iris!

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.650
Escaping now!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:38.140
<i>This method uses the Dragon's Breath,</i>

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:42.300
<i>inverting its direction and attributes 
to destroy the dragon with its own spell.</i>

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.130
<i>But it does take time to activate.</i>

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.860
Iris! Watch where you're running!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.470
<i>That enormous fool!</i>

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:58.290
<i>No matter how tough Iris might be, 
she can't fully tank a direct hit like that!</i>

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.490
Iris, get down!

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:00.460
Right!

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.570
I-Is it over?

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.840
Dispatch successful, right?

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:24.050
But where are the others?

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.500
I'm right here.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:27.930
Matty!

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.410
A-Are you all right?

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:33.810
Yes. A human can survive getting thrown 
a hundred meters or so.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:35.680
Uh, I don't think we can.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.140
Got the magistone!

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.440
Iris!

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:40.480
Any injuries?

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:43.460
All good, thanks to you, Matthias!

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:47.590
<i>It was touch-and-go for a minute there, 
but I'd say she passed the test!</i>

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:48.830
Iris!

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.320
Yes?

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:54.070
Would you like 
to join our party officially?

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.360
A-Are you sure?

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.410
Of course I am.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:58.610
I'm all for it!

00:16:58.610 --> 00:16:59.900
As am I!

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:02.450
Iris would make a powerful ally!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.210
It's decided, then.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.320
Thank you very much!

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:09.820
So there's something else 
we need to take care of...

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:11.000
Eh?

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:17.310
We need training 
to improve our party's teamwork.

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:20.140
But why did you ruin 
the school grounds like this?

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:24.200
Iris needs to get used 
to her human body.

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:27.650
She's particularly bad 
about watching her footing.

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:32.690
Training on uneven ground like this 
should help her establish some muscle memory.

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:36.050
I see! A very smart idea, Matthias!

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:38.530
Okay, let's start the training!

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:48.160
You can't hit me that easily!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.720
I did it! First point goes to me!

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.160
Iris! To protect the shell on your head,

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.350
you'll want to dodge 
with the least movement possible!

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:01.350
Very well!

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:06.270
The least movement possible... 
The least movement possible...

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.310
Yeah!

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:14.330
Human bodies really are so inconvenient.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:15.490
Ready to quit, then?

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:18.740
I'm not done yet!

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:23.240
What should I do, Matty?

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:27.580
Let's have you make some new equipment 
to level up your enchantments.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:30.100
I'll want you making my weapon 
this time, too.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.370
I'll do my best!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.700
I promise I'll make you 
some very fine equipment!

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:36.330
S-Sure...

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:39.300
We'll start with a sword for me.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:45.770
We recovered a number of resources 
from that dragon, in addition to the magistone.

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:48.120
A dragon's claw and some mithril.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:50.920
As for the spells themselves, 
let's see...

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:53.770
Sunder Steel, Enhance Edge, 
Magic Slash,

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:57.090
Shockwave Blade, Enhance Hardness, 
Enhance Fortitude,

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:59.870
Resist Heat, 
and Resist Abrasion should—

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:03.870
Eight spells? 
How do I add all those?!

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.910
You're right. It's impossible 
to put all eight on one blade.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.730
So we'll layer them!

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:09.830
"Layer them"?

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:12.740
Split the blade into five parts.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:14.570
Put the dragon's claw in the center,

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:17.900
then add two layers 
of mithril plates on each side.

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:21.030
Imagine adding four spells to each part,

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:24.260
then it all coming together at the end.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.770
I see...

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:27.300
What an amazing idea!

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:28.830
Let's try it, then!

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:29.680
Very well!

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:38.860
I did it!

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.800
Though it feels unreal.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:42.210
Great work!

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:44.660
Now we'll make a sword for you.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:51.000
I'm getting the hang 
of these minimal movements.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:57.130
You dodged one, 
but that's not the end!

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.300
You've got a long way to go!

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:00.830
I let my guard down.

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:03.250
But I won't get hit again!

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:05.210
Seems that you're making progress.

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:06.050
Yes!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:07.180
Come this way.

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:10.140
Lurie made new weapons.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.040
First up, Lurie.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:16.140
Okay! Here I go!

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.030
I did it!

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:25.370
Next, Alma!

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:28.240
That sword's pretty great,

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.250
but I'll bet this bow is, too!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.400
W-Wow!

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:36.830
And last, Iris!

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:39.800
Is this a spear?

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:43.590
The blade's on the dull side, 
in deference to your power.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:45.800
Here I go!

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:01.070
Now I can really give it all I've got!

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:04.690
Unlike a sword, you can get some decent 
attacks just by flailing a spear around.

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:06.240
Should be easy enough for you to use.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:09.200
Okay, let's do even more training!

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.680
Yeah!

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:11.490
All right...

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:14.320
Let's try me against the three of you.

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:16.460
Give me your best shot!

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:22.630
<i>I have a new member in my party.</i>

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:26.090
<i>The popularity of wordless casting 
is spreading.</i>

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:31.500
<i>Once we finish the barrier around the kingdom 
and drive away those demons,</i>

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:33.550
<i>I'll have no more need to stay here.</i>

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:39.110
If things go well, 
I'll be leaving this school soon enough.

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.460
Wait for me...

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:52.110
Foolish members of the human race.

00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:28.220
I'm tired from training!

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:30.730
I know! Let's play rock-paper-scissors 
to see who has to go shopping!

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:31.740
What a good idea!

00:23:31.740 --> 00:23:32.540
Let's do it!

00:23:32.540 --> 00:23:34.790
Okay! First comes rock...

00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:35.610
Rock, paper—

00:23:35.610 --> 00:23:36.250
Rock!

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:37.060
Eek!

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:40.020
The wind generated by Iris's punch 
blew everyone away!

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Episode 6
 The Strongest Sage Leaves the School.</b>
